// The registers of the Radeon RX 580's graphics block (GFX8, Polaris 10) as
// Mesa's register database has them. GENERATED by
// tools/gpu_registers_generate.py (do not edit: generate it again; README.md
// beside it says how a register is added) from Mesa mesa-24.0.0's
// src/amd/registers/gfx8.json and the GFX8 entries of
// registers-manually-defined.json, whose sha256 are
//   gfx8.json                       225dcbb9c4d16cc4c79d48e1b91d19ab71afa24f6a14e3613ddc49379c08d1bb
//   registers-manually-defined.json 0e1f10a943eeb840fb55d1f1fb89e1a998893659f14195b6c0ca9869cdc9e83a
//
// Every register of the database, 1496 (1491 of gfx8.json, 5 of Mesa's own
// additions), with every field (3443) and all 96 enums. A register is its
// BYTE offset in the MMIO space (the database's "at", as Mesa and the Vulkan
// driver's packets count it; Linux's and the kernel's dword index is a
// quarter of it: the block modules beside this one). NAME__FIELD is a
// field's mask, NAME__FIELD__SHIFT its lowest bit, and a field that takes an
// enum names it; an enum is a struct of its values, named as the database
// names it.
//
// WHERE THE DATABASE AND LINUX'S HEADERS DIFFER (gca/gfx_8_0_d.h,
// _sh_mask.h, _enum.h, and oss/oss_3_0 for Mesa's additions), kept apart:
// the database's numbers here, Linux's in its block's module.
// 1464 registers at the same place in both (1459 in gfx_8_0, 5 in oss_3_0),
// 3441 fields with the same bits, 622 enum values the same.
// - 32 registers the database places among the MMIO words at four times the
// number Linux gives them in the SQ's index space (its ixNAME, reached
// through SQ_IND_INDEX and SQ_IND_DATA, never an MMIO word): SQ_WAVE_MODE
// SQ_WAVE_STATUS SQ_WAVE_TRAPSTS SQ_WAVE_HW_ID SQ_WAVE_GPR_ALLOC
// SQ_WAVE_LDS_ALLOC SQ_WAVE_IB_STS SQ_WAVE_PC_LO SQ_WAVE_PC_HI
// SQ_WAVE_INST_DW0 SQ_WAVE_INST_DW1 SQ_WAVE_IB_DBG0 SQ_WAVE_IB_DBG1
// SQ_WAVE_TBA_LO SQ_WAVE_TBA_HI SQ_WAVE_TMA_LO SQ_WAVE_TMA_HI SQ_WAVE_TTMP0
// SQ_WAVE_TTMP1 SQ_WAVE_TTMP2 SQ_WAVE_TTMP3 SQ_WAVE_TTMP4 SQ_WAVE_TTMP5
// SQ_WAVE_TTMP6 SQ_WAVE_TTMP7 SQ_WAVE_TTMP8 SQ_WAVE_TTMP9 SQ_WAVE_TTMP10
// SQ_WAVE_TTMP11 SQ_WAVE_M0 SQ_WAVE_EXEC_LO SQ_WAVE_EXEC_HI; gfx_8_0.mlx has
// them as Linux has them (ixNAME).
// COVERAGE, no number in question: 2 fields only the database names
// (SQ_IMG_SAMP_WORD3.UPGRADED_DEPTH, bits 29..29,
// SQ_THREAD_TRACE_MASK.RANDOM_SEED, bits 16..31); 754 registers the database
// leaves without fields to which Linux gives one field that is the whole
// word (SQ_WAVE_PC_LO.PC_LO SQ_WAVE_INST_DW0.INST_DW0
// SQ_WAVE_INST_DW1.INST_DW1 ...); 0 fields only Linux names of registers the
// database describes; 11 enums only the database has, by names of its own
// (CB_COLOR_DCC_CONTROL__MAX_UNCOMPRESSED_BLOCK_SIZE
// CB_COLOR_DCC_CONTROL__MIN_COMPRESSED_BLOCK_SIZE CLIP_RULE EXCP_EN
// FLOAT_MODE PA_SU_SC_MODE_CNTL__POLYMODE_FRONT_PTYPE
// PA_SU_SC_MODE_CNTL__POLY_MODE PA_SU_VTX_CNTL__ROUND_MODE QUANT_MODE ROP3
// VGT_HS_OFFCHIP_PARAM__OFFCHIP_GRANULARITY).

